// tests/pass/327_arena_stale_read.dva — issue #126: reading inner string after restore aborts with E4010
//
// A block value built inside the block's own restore scope must be copied out
// with '++' (see 264_addr_arena_safety); reading it uncopied afterwards aborts.
// (Assigning the inner string straight to the outer s' now keeps it alive:
// the loop body writes outer state, so it no longer restores the arena.)
#use io

s' = ++""
0..1 @ i =>
   s' =
      t = "inner" + "_value"
      t
   io::out(s')

io::out("FAIL: should have aborted")
